reener.com/v2/announcements/view/11708465","src":"ai"}],"recent_en":"Semico Capital's Q1 net profit for the period ended 30 September 2026 fell 44% year-on-year to RM732,000 despite 4.7% revenue growth, and it declared a first interim dividend of 0.15 sen per share. The company opened a new family entertainment centre at Berjaya Times Square on 3 November and held its 2nd AGM on 24 November, with all resolutions passed.","notable_en":["Declared a first interim dividend of 0.15 sen per share, with ex-date on 8 December 2026.","Opened a new family entertainment centre at Berjaya Times Square.","All resolutions were passed by shareholders at the 2nd Annual General Meeting."],"risks_en":["CEO Tai Lee Chuen acquired a total of 3,148,000 shares on 4 and 5 November during the closed period.","Tai Lee Chuen transferred 34,000,000 shares to pledged securities accounts on 30 October during the closed period."],"earnings_en":"For Q1 ended 30 September 2026, net profit fell 44% year-on-year to RM732,000 while revenue grew 4.7%. For the prior financial year ended 30 June 2026, revenue was RM8,032,000 with net profit of RM337,000, a net margin of 4.2%, and revenue declined 12.7% quarter-on-quarter."}